# shadcn components

Build UI with the shadcn components in `@/components/ui`. Do not hand-roll buttons, inputs, dialogs, menus, cards, or other controls that already exist there.

```tsx
// Bad
<button className="rounded-full bg-primary px-3 py-2">Save</button>
<input className="w-full rounded-md border px-2" />

// Good
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import { Input } from "@/components/ui/input";

<Button type="submit">Save</Button>
<Input />
```

Style a link as a button with `buttonVariants`, the same way the header and recipe pages do:

```tsx
import Link from "next/link";
import { buttonVariants } from "@/components/ui/button";

<Link href="/recipes/new" className={buttonVariants()}>
  New recipe
</Link>
```

If the component is missing from `components/ui`, add it with the project CLI. Do not copy a component in by hand.

```bash
bunx --bun shadcn@latest add dialog
```

- Import primitives from `@/components/ui/<name>`. Compose them in feature components; leave files in `components/ui` as generated.
- Use `lucide-react` for icons.
- Match `components.json`: `base-luma` style, taupe base color, CSS variables.
